# gdlint configuration (gdtoolkit). Read by `gdlint` when it is run from the
# project root; every key not listed here keeps the tool's default.
#
# Only the file-length limit is raised. The biome self-test is one file by design:
# it builds its own segments, layers and track, needs no imported artwork, prints a
# single summary line and is run by hand or in CI with one command. Splitting it at
# an arbitrary line count would cost a reader more than it saves, and the file grows
# with every behaviour worth a regression test - the draw-order arithmetic took it
# past 1400, the end-to-end ranking test past 1500, and the per-prop priorities past
# 1650. The cap moves rather than the tests being cut; a fourth move should come with
# splitting the suite, which is a project decision and not a lint one.
max-file-lines: 1750
